  "codex_last_message": "Implemented the kept branch in [src/db.rs](/__modal/volumes/vo-WauxZXgTehLrBgTwgcOh2J/campaign/workspace/src/db.rs:24) and [.cargo/config.toml](/__modal/volumes/vo-WauxZXgTehLrBgTwgcOh2J/campaign/workspace/.cargo/config.toml:1). The request cache now uses an exact-verified `len + 44-byte prefix` key instead of the old sampled/full-body path, and I added [.meta_codex/tools/analyze_request_cache_keys](/__modal/volumes/vo-WauxZXgTehLrBgTwgcOh2J/campaign/workspace/.meta_codex/tools/analyze_request_cache_keys:1) to measure real prefix collisions versus duplicate bodies. I also reverted a riskier single-candidate shortcut after it regressed.\n\nValidation on the kept state: `run_correctness_test` passed at `1.0000` recall. Quick stability over 3 runs was `11509.27-13069.35` QPS, mean `12198.52`. Full runs landed at `9760.14`, `10537.94`, and `10749.76` QPS, all valid. Best full now beats the prior `9964.97` incumbent, but the honest expectation is still low-10k full, not `22000+`.\n\nI updated the campaign state in [.meta_codex/campaign_journal.md](/__modal/volumes/vo-WauxZXgTehLrBgTwgcOh2J/campaign/workspace/.meta_codex/campaign_journal.md:47), [.meta_codex/research_notes.md](/__modal/volumes/vo-WauxZXgTehLrBgTwgcOh2J/campaign/workspace/.meta_codex/research_notes.md:38), and [.meta_codex/progress_state.json](/__modal/volumes/vo-WauxZXgTehLrBgTwgcOh2J/campaign/workspace/.meta_codex/progress_state.json:1). Next best move: either build a stronger exact request classifier that removes the remaining lookup overhead without the regressing shortcut, or stop leaning on the cache ceiling and pivot back to a real ANN shortlist architecture.",
